/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  Membrane: the NanoFiltran example membrane -- CASE-LOCAL, HYPOTHETICAL.

  The pore parameters of the example shipped with NanoFiltran (Geraldes &
  Alves, J. Membr. Sci. 321 (2008) 172-182; its INPUT.XLS, sections 3):
    membrane charge         -30 mol/m3 (eq/m3)
    pore radius             0.40 nm
    active layer thickness  2.5 um   -> porosityOverThickness 1/2.5e-6
    pore dielectric const.  60
  They describe NO commercial membrane and were measured on none: they are
  the program's worked example, used here so that two implementations of
  one model can be compared on the same inputs.

  NanoFiltran writes the ENP flux per unit PORE area with the thickness
  delta: j = -K_d D dc/dx - ... + K_c J_v c, j = J_v c_p.  Choupo writes it
  per unit MEMBRANE area with A_k/dx; the two are the same equations when
  A_k/dx = 1/delta, which is what porosityOverThickness states.

  A_w is not read by the props bench (it imposes J_v); a value is carried
  because the record grammar requires one.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

name           NanoFiltranExample;
kind           NF;
manufacturer   "none (NanoFiltran's worked example)";

A_w            1.0e-5  m/s/bar;     // not read at an imposed J_v

poreModel
{
    poreRadius             4.0e-10;   // m
    porosityOverThickness  4.0e5;     // 1/m  (= 1/2.5e-6 m)
    chargeDensity          -30;       // mol/m3, SIGNED
    poreDielectric         60;        // [-]
}
